From 31aa415eaf8460b58b11c9cba4722ecd23b6d617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:37:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] SolidArc: Vulkan DeviceRasterExchange behind
 RasterExchange (matcap shaders, pick plane, SSAA), raster/D3D11/tool logs

- Presentation/DeviceRasterExchange.{h,cpp}: one render pass per target (RGBA16F linear colour, R32_UINT pick, D32 depth),
  dynamic-UBO view/draw records, lazy pipeline variants (depth/pick/overlay), synchronous readback, GPU timestamps.
  Borrows the host's VkDevice (Frontier.exe) or opens its own headless device.
- Presentation/Shaders/Device*.slang: real-Slang entry points over the existing SurfaceRaster/LineRaster/PointRaster/LatticeProjection
  bodies (analytic matcap). Shared bodies now use MatrixColumn() instead of mirror-only .m[] indexing (software output unchanged, hash-verified).
- RasterExchange gains AssignSamples/QuerySamples/QueryBackend/QueryTargetMilliseconds; ConsoleHost::SeatRaster swaps the backend.
- Logs: [SolidArcRaster] backend/resolution/ms, [SolidArcDevice], [SolidArcPresent] D3D11 hardware vs WARP + adapter, [SolidArcTool] events.
- Build: BuildSolidArcApplication.py lowers Device*.slang with slangc (column-major) and defines SOLIDARC_VULKAN_RASTER;
  optional SOLIDARC_VULKAN_RASTER CMake option. GPU-unverified.
